in our exclusive interview brianna  taylor's boyfriend told us  about his struggles with the emotional  trauma of her death kenneth walker was  with taylor the night she was killed by  louisville police officers  during a narcotics raid in march now  police were investigating another man  neither walker nor taylor had a criminal  history and no ill  no illegal drugs were found in the home  walker told us his love story with  taylor began  actually on twitter we went to the  louisville home to talk to him and his  parents  who considered taylor family they say  that she brought  joy into everybody's life  kenny i want to know about brianna  taylor what was it about her that  attracted you to her  she was funny like me and i can see from  twitter she played a lot just like me  always joking  always laughing come on  these two how did you know that she was  the one for you  it was friends for a long time before  ever  evolved into any anything else  so i think that's how i knew she was the  one we was too good at being friends  but it ended up working out and  finally we was getting it together right  getting it together like you thought i  could marry you get it together  that kind of thing that was definitely  in the talks definitely had a  baby names and everything like like  cambrie oh that's kenneth and brianna  together  walker says he and taylor were  collecting their favorite items for the  family they hope  to build like this pair of mini air  jordans for the baby  they want it together looking at these  baby shoes  what do they mean to me it means it's  something that's never going to happen  walker's parents volitia and kenneth  walker jr have been supporting their son  through his grief  and want justice for brianna taylor the  woman who would have been their  daughter-in-law  i say it all the time you know as a mom  you know you want the best mate for your  children  and she just completed us she completed  the family  on the night of the police raid kenneth  says in his fear and panic  he called his mother for help before  calling 9-1-1  volicia walker rushed to the scene and  recordings released by louisville police  show  that she spoke to officers about what  her son told her  that night he called me and said  mama they kicked in the door they keep  there no i don't know what's going on  it's just one of those calls as as a mom  that we hope we never get  at one o'clock in the morning he  couldn't tell you what had happened  could he he didn't know  i didn't hear anything at first in the  background i just heard him screaming  and crying  what's your biggest concern as we sit  here today about kenneth  it's hard i'm mama i can see things  about him that he doesn't even realize  whereas when they were little kids if  you had a bump on it you could fix it  i could blow it but i can't fix this  i've only listened to that 911 call  once or twice and it took me months to  listen to it and the thing is  his whole life i've always been there to  help him or to be there for him  and i couldn't help him because he was  considered a suspect in the beginning  right and i mean you know think about it  reality is he still was suspecting their  mind  he's still their scapegoat in the chaos  that followed the death of brianna  taylor on march 13th  walker was indicted for the attempted  murder of a police officer  in may those charges were dropped  without prejudice which means the case  can be refiled in the future  for kenneth and his family it is a stark  possibility  that they never could have imagined you  know the simple lessons that we teach  them  that we hold true as parents  the lessons that we treat you know ain't  nothing good for you going on at the  streets stay at home  here you are this one time you at home  and you get in the worst trouble you've  ever been at home  at home and you did nothing wrong but do  what you were taught to do  be a man protect your family  tell the truth hey stop playing with it  it's like march 13th every day pretty  much  i never got to say bye so  that makes a big deal makes a big  difference when it first happened  you're labeled a suspect brianna's  labeled a suspect and the police officer  who was shot  is labeled a victim what do you make of  that  she usually had goals when you black and  deal with police  that's all i think of that i don't  necessarily even see this as a black  white issue it became that  after they figured it out but this is a  right and wrong issue  it don't matter if he was blue pink  purple you know white black  doesn't really matter it could have been  elderly people in there it could have  been kids it could have been anything  so it was just wrong all the way around  the board no matter who was in there  but it definitely turned into a black  and white thing when i walked out  yeah we should say that neither you or  brianna taylor had a  criminal history of violence or  drugs i guess that doesn't matter to  them you know people like to skip over  that part  where do you go from here i mean i look  at you and i just see  so much pain and rightfully so do you  have friends who are helping you  i i actually do have a therapist i  probably need to i'm gonna  i'll be talking to him a lot more yeah  but  i really don't agree with therapy but  you got to try everything to try to  be okay  [Applause]  when you hear the chance say her name  what does that mean to you when you hear  that  it means she's getting the respect that  she deserves  now that's the least that could happen  what does justice look like for you for  brianna taylor brianna taylor sitting  right here next to me  that's the only justice for me wow  none of the officers involved were  charged for brianna taylor's death both  the louisville metro police department  and attorneys for the three individual  officers involved  declined our request for interview or  comment on this case and another thing  that was really touching  when we were at her house because he  couldn't go the funeral because he was  in prison for attempted murder of a  police officer  briana taylor's mother has given him a  little urn of her ashes  and they showed us the ashes i didn't i  didn't show it on camera but just to be  able to  hold it and see it was very very i  i could physically feel that yes of  course it means a lot to him to have it  but  there's just so many inconsistencies in  this story he is such a  and he is such a compelling interview  and as we we were talking in the  break but one of the things i said to  you was this started with a warrant  yes that clearly was misguided they were  at the wrong place  and that's what i want to know how that  warrant got there yeah that's why  candice says it's not a black white  issue to him it's  right right or wrong right or wrong  issue and you understand why he reacted  the way he did because he and  this is the thing his story has never  changed from that very first night  he's been very consistent about he had  no idea what was happening and to your  point about the warrant  his his attorneys were there of course  while we were talking to him and they  they can  fill us in on how that war it came to be  and why this story does seem to have  gone awry  listen it started out playing uno and  watching a movie yeah and at the end of  the night only one person has survived  that  and now can we say there's nothing  sadder or more tragic than a pair of  baby shoes never worn  tony there were so many things it was a  very very very tough day

